WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.486
Start with the division and eligibility rules in the round announcement.

00:00:04.486 --> 00:00:07.976
Division four often offers an accessible starting point.

00:00:07.976 --> 00:00:12.400
Virtual participation lets you practice a past round against the clock.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.266
In a points-based round, the time of acceptance can affect the score.

00:00:17.266 --> 00:00:23.089
In an ICPC-style round, teams are ranked first by problems solved, then by penalty time.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.140
Check the rules for your event.

00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:29.421
Passing pretests is provisional in rounds that use them.

00:00:29.421 --> 00:00:34.264
A later system test can expose a missed boundary or a slow approach.

00:00:34.264 --> 00:00:37.753
Try the smallest input and a case near the limit.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.787
After the round, find the first assumption that failed.

00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:47.970
Make a small counterexample, explain the fix, and solve the problem again before moving on.
